WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.510
Have you seen the Liquid Death water company?

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:06.290
Yeah, this company is valued at $700 million.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.550
They literally sell water in a can.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.690
And yes, it's in this like “tall boy”
can.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.960
And yes, it's got like the over-the-top death
metal aesthetic, but it's just water.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.511
I think what this shows us is that Liquid
Death understands how human brains work.

00:00:18.511 --> 00:00:22.100
We think we're like rational people who go
out and, like, buy things because they're

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.130
useful to us.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.460
Like we're going to go buy water because we
need water.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.680
That's not what's happening here.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.500
They're nakedly showing just how powerful
branding is because they're getting people

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.670
to buy a product that is objectively worthless
because it looks kind of cool and edgy and

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.090
weird and counterculture.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.280
Liquid Death is about signaling to others
and maybe yourself a little bit that you are

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.739
anti-establishment and that's freaking brilliant.

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:48.329
Whoever's in charge of the marketing over
at Liquid Death deserves an A+.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:51.930
And now, after thinking about this, it's like
I can't stop thinking of all the other things

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.110
that I purchase in my life that aren't about
the product, but are about what buying the

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.350
product says about me.

